%%{init: {"flowchart": {"rankSpacing": 30, "nodeSpacing": 24}}}%%
flowchart LR
    accTitle: Longitudinal layer for five fixed sites
    accDescr: A new report is normalised to reads per million classified, compared against the same site's own history when at least three prior runs exist, otherwise against the other sites, and appended to a small stored table that feeds the next run.
    N(["new report"]) --> RPM["reads/M<br/>per taxid"]
    RPM --> SELF{"≥ 3 prior<br/>runs here?"}
    SELF -- yes --> Z["own history<br/>robust z ≥ 3"]
    SELF -- no --> X["other sites<br/>≥ 5× median"]
    Z --> OUT["site<br/>conclusion"]
    X --> OUT
    OUT --> ST[("stored<br/>rows")]
    ST -. next run .-> SELF
    classDef gate fill:#e8e4f3,stroke:#5b4b8a,color:#241a3d
    classDef term fill:#dff0d8,stroke:#3c763d,color:#1b3a1f
    class RPM,SELF,Z,X gate
    class OUT,ST term
